<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Lagos (1759)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1759">1759</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Lagos · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lagos">Lagos</a> was a naval battle fought in 1759 off the coast of Portugal during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a>. A British fleet under Admiral Edward Boscawen defeated a French squadron trying to leave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>. The defeat contributed to French naval losses that year and weakened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>'s ability to defend its overseas empire.</p></div>
